Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: v4l2: release buffer cache on queue failure

V4L2VideoDevice::queueBuffer() reserves an entry in V4L2BufferCache before
validating the FrameBuffer and before issuing VIDIOC_QBUF.  Every validation
failure and a failed QBUF then leave that entry marked busy even though the
buffer was never queued.  A later streamOff() cannot find the entry in
queuedBuffers_ and aborts on the cache_->isEmpty() assertion.

The Surface IPU4P fail-closed stream path exposed the QBUF case: the kernel
returned EIO for follow-up buffers after STREAMON failed, and PipeWire then
hit the assertion while stopping the libcamera stream.

Validate the buffer before reserving a cache entry, and release the entry if
VIDIOC_QBUF fails.  This preserves the successful queue path while ensuring
that every post-reservation failure has an explicit rollback.

---
 src/libcamera/v4l2_videodevice.cpp | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/v4l2_videodevice.cpp b/src/libcamera/v4l2_videodevice.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/v4l2_videodevice.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/v4l2_videodevice.cpp
@@ -1639,11 +1639,6 @@ int V4L2VideoDevice::queueBuffer(FrameBuffer *buffer)
 		return -ENOENT;
 	}
 
-	ret = cache_->get(*buffer);
-	if (ret < 0)
-		return ret;
-
-	buf.index = ret;
 	buf.type = bufferType_;
 	buf.memory = memoryType_;
 	buf.field = V4L2_FIELD_NONE;
@@ -1747,10 +1742,16 @@ int V4L2VideoDevice::queueBuffer(FrameBuffer *buffer)
 		buf.timestamp.tv_usec = (metadata.timestamp / 1000) % 1000000;
 	}
 
+	ret = cache_->get(*buffer);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	buf.index = ret;
 	LOG(V4L2, Debug) << "Queueing buffer " << buf.index;
 
 	ret = ioctl(VIDIOC_QBUF, &buf);
 	if (ret < 0) {
+		cache_->put(buf.index);
 		LOG(V4L2, Error)
 			<< "Failed to queue buffer " << buf.index << ": "
 			<< strerror(-ret);
